From: Gigachad Enthusiast <32457258-AreteMaxxing@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:37:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Graphics paging: no tile-art rebuild on page-in, at most
 GRAPHICS_PAGING_MAX_IN set-ups per update

A fast zoom-out at turn 108 of a huge 20-civilization game set up 918
plots, 6 units and 2 cities again in one pass, four times the most
before, and the game crashed. Each of those plots also rebuilt its
tile art (RebuildTileArt), which paging never removes. A plot that
comes back now gets its feature symbol again without the tile-art
rebuild (CvPlot::updateFeatureSymbolEntity), and one update sets up at
most GRAPHICS_PAGING_MAX_IN (100) plots, units and cities again; the
rest follow at the next updates, in the same window. Page-outs are not
limited. Docs/GRAPHICS_PAGING.md describes the crash and the change.

Serves: P20
