+### The crash while zooming (!62)
+
+A 20-civilization game on a huge Europe map, played under Proton, crashed at turn 108 while the
+player zoomed in and out fast to test paging. `GraphicsPaging.log`:
+- **Before:** 105 passes set up 2,282 plots, 21 units and 7 cities again; the most in one pass
+  was 238 plots, 2 units and 1 city.
+- **Last:** the window grew from 60 x 43 to 60 x 65 plots in 0.3 s, and one pass set up 918 plots,
+  6 units and 2 cities again. Each of the 918 plots also had its tile art rebuilt
+  (`RebuildTileArt`), which paging never removes.
+- **After:** no further pass is logged; `PythonDbg.log` goes on about 4 s longer, with no error.
+
+No crash address was obtained. `claude/paging-zoom` removes the tile-art rebuilds and spreads a large
+set-up over several updates; whether this was the cause is for the game to show.
+
